{"id":"en-44","title":"OneLaser Firmware Upgrade Guide (For Win-Only Users)","family":"software","topic":"downloads","read_minutes":3,"source_url":"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-update/window-users","source_updated_at":"2025-11-28T07:16:33.281Z","body_html":"<div><h2 id=\"firmware-upgrade-guide-for-win-only-users\"> Firmware Upgrade Guide (For Win-Only Users)</h2>\n<h2 id=\"h-1-x-series\"> 1. X Series</h2><div>\n\n</div><h3 id=\"h-11-updating-control-board-firmware\"> 1.1 Updating Control Board Firmware</h3>\n<h4 id=\"h-111-updating-control-board-firmware-via-rdworks\"> 1.1.1 Updating Control Board Firmware via RDWorks</h4><div>\n\n</div><p>1.Install the RDWorks program on your computer.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片7.png\" alt=\"RDWorks installation window for X Series firmware upgrade\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片8.png\" alt=\"RDWorks setup interface on Windows\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片9.png\" alt=\"RDWorks software after installation for firmware updating\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>2.Connect the device to the computer using a data cable and start RDWorks.</p><div>\n\n</div><p>3.Click &quot;System Setting&quot; - &quot;Controller&quot; to enter the controller upgrade interface. Enter &quot;rd8888&quot; in the &quot;Vendor password&quot; input field and click the &quot;Input&quot; button to confirm the password.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片10.png\" alt=\"RDWorks controller settings menu for firmware update\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片11.png\" alt=\"Vendor password entry screen in RDWorks\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>4.Click &quot;Upgrade firmware&quot;. In the pop-up window, find and select the corresponding motherboard firmware upgrade file, wait and confirm that the upgrade is complete.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片14.png\" alt=\"Selecting firmware file in RDWorks for X Series upgrade\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片15.png\" alt=\"RDWorks firmware upgrade progress confirmation window\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>5.Click &quot;OK&quot; to close the prompt window. Restart the device.</p><div>\n\n</div><p> </p>\n<p><strong>Caution:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Be sure to select an upgrade file that matches the controller. (You can check the bar code label on the motherboard to determine whether it is new or old. The old motherboard number has &quot;1G&quot; and the new motherboard does not.)</strong></li>\n</ul><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片16.png\" alt=\"Barcode label on laser motherboard identifying controller version\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片17.png\" alt=\"Comparison image of old and new laser controller boards\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片18.png\" alt=\"Laser control board showing firmware compatibility markings\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><ul>\n  <li>Cannot upgrade using a firmware file lower than the current version.</li>\n  <li>Restart the device after the upgrade.</li>\n</ul><div>\n\n</div><p> </p><div>\n\n</div><h4 id=\"h-112-updating-control-board-firmware-via-makerboost\"> 1.1.2 Updating Control Board Firmware via MakerBoost</h4>\n<p>(Panel firmware upgrade support will be added in a future update)</p><div>\n\n</div><p>1.Launch MakerBoost and click &quot;Switch&quot; to connect to the XRF/XT machine.</p>\n<p>2.Open &quot;Settings&quot;, select &quot;Vendor Setting&quot;, and enter the password: TL9501.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片20.png\" alt=\"MakerBoost vendor settings screen for X Series firmware update\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片21.png\" alt=\"MakerBoost system upgrade menu for laser control board\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>3.After clicking &quot;System&quot;, select &quot;Upgrade&quot;. Upload the corresponding device firmware file. Wait for the upgrade process to complete. Power off the device completely, then restart it to finalize the controller firmware upgrade.</p><div>\n\n</div><p> </p>\n<p><strong>Caution:</strong></p><div>\n\n</div><ul>\n  <li><strong>MUST select a firmware file EXACTLY matching your controller model. (The selection method is the same as mentioned above)</strong></li>\n  <li>NEVER attempt to downgrade (e.g. installing firmware older than the current version).</li>\n  <li>During the upgrade process, do <strong>NOT</strong> turn off the device, unplug the cable, or press any buttons.</li>\n</ul><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片22.png\" alt=\"Firmware upgrade progress bar in MakerBoost for X Series\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片23.png\" alt=\"Successful firmware update message on MakerBoost\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p> </p><div>\n\n</div><h3 id=\"h-12-updating-panel-firmware-via-tf-card\"> 1.2 Updating Panel Firmware via TF Card</h3><div>\n\n</div><p>1.Use a blank TF card, a card reader, and a docking station to connect the TF card to your computer.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片25.png\" alt=\"TF card and reader setup for firmware update\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>2.Open “Disk Utility” and format the TF card to ensure the file system is FAT32.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片26.png\" alt=\"Formatting TF card to FAT32 for panel firmware update\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>3.Extract the front panel firmware upgrade files to the root directory of the TF card. Then safely eject the TF card from your computer and remove it.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片30.png\" alt=\"Extracting panel firmware files to TF card\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片31.png\" alt=\"TF card directory containing panel firmware update files\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>4.Ensure the device is powered off completely. Remove the right-side protective cover of the control panel, then insert the TF card into the TF card slot at the bottom of the control panel.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片32.png\" alt=\"Inserting TF card into X Series front panel for firmware update\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/firmware-upgrade-3/图片33.png\" alt=\"X Series panel showing TF card detected for upgrade\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>5.Power on the device. The front panel will automatically begin updating. When the screen displays “SD CARD PROCESS...END!”, the upgrade is complete. Power off the device, remove the TF card, and then power it on again.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/firmware-upgrade-3/图片34.png\" alt=\"Front panel showing SD card firmware update progress\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/firmware-upgrade-3/图片35.png\" alt=\"Panel displaying SD CARD PROCESS END after firmware update\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p> </p><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"h-2-hydra-series\"> 2. Hydra Series</h2><div>\n\n</div><h3 id=\"h-21-updating-main-control-board-and-panel-firmware-via-usb-drive\"> 2.1 Updating Main Control Board and Panel Firmware via USB Drive</h3><div>\n\n</div><p>1.Copy the main control board and HMI upgrade files to a USB drive and insert it into the device&#x27;s control panel. On the touchscreen, navigate to “Menu” → “U disk”.</p>\n<p>2.Click on “Controller” and “HMI” to begin each firmware update.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片1.png\" alt=\"Hydra Series touchscreen showing USB firmware update menu\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片2.png\" alt=\"Hydra controller firmware update selection screen\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片3.png\" alt=\"Hydra Series firmware update progress screen\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片4.png\" alt=\"Selecting HMI firmware upgrade from USB drive\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片5.png\" alt=\"Hydra HMI firmware update progress bar\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片6.png\" alt=\"Hydra Series firmware update completed successfully\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Note:</strong> <strong>A system restart is required after each individual upgrade is completed.</strong></p><div>\n\n</div><p> </p><div>\n\n</div><h3 id=\"h-22-updating-main-control-board-and-panel-firmware-via-rdworks\"> 2.2 Updating Main Control Board and Panel Firmware via RDWorks</h3><div>\n\n</div><p>1.Install the RDWorks program on your computer.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片7.png\" alt=\"RDWorks installation window for Hydra firmware update\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片8.png\" alt=\"RDWorks setup screen on Windows PC\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片9.png\" alt=\"RDWorks interface after installation for Hydra updates\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>2.Connect the device to the computer using a data cable and start RDWorks.</p><div>\n\n</div><p>3.Click &quot;System Setting&quot; - &quot;Controller&quot; to enter the controller upgrade interface. Enter &quot;rd8888&quot; in the &quot;Vendor password&quot; field and click &quot;Input&quot;.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片10.png\" alt=\"Hydra controller upgrade menu in RDWorks\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片11.png\" alt=\"Vendor password window inside RDWorks\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>4.Click &quot;Upgrade HMI&quot; and select the correct HMI firmware file.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片12.png\" alt=\"Selecting HMI firmware file in RDWorks for Hydra\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片13.png\" alt=\"Hydra HMI firmware updating inside RDWorks\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>5.Click &quot;OK&quot; and restart the device.</p><div>\n\n</div><p>6.Return to “System Setting - Controller” and click &quot;Upgrade firmware&quot; to update the motherboard firmware.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片14.png\" alt=\"Choosing motherboard firmware file for Hydra upgrade\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片15.png\" alt=\"Firmware upgrade progress confirmation for Hydra controller\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>7.Click &quot;OK&quot; and restart the device.</p>\n</div>","headings":[{"level":1,"id":"firmware-upgrade-guide-for-win-only-users","text":"Firmware Upgrade Guide (For Win-Only Users)"},{"level":2,"id":"h-1-x-series","text":"1. X Series"},{"level":3,"id":"h-11-updating-control-board-firmware","text":"1.1 Updating Control Board Firmware"},{"level":4,"id":"h-111-updating-control-board-firmware-via-rdworks","text":"1.1.1 Updating Control Board Firmware via RDWorks"},{"level":4,"id":"h-112-updating-control-board-firmware-via-makerboost","text":"1.1.2 Updating Control Board Firmware via MakerBoost"},{"level":3,"id":"h-12-updating-panel-firmware-via-tf-card","text":"1.2 Updating Panel Firmware via TF Card"},{"level":2,"id":"h-2-hydra-series","text":"2. Hydra Series"},{"level":3,"id":"h-21-updating-main-control-board-and-panel-firmware-via-usb-drive","text":"2.1 Updating Main Control Board and Panel Firmware via USB Drive"},{"level":3,"id":"h-22-updating-main-control-board-and-panel-firmware-via-rdworks","text":"2.2 Updating Main Control Board and Panel Firmware via RDWorks"}],"technical_version":"unknown"}